## Fetching a Screen's HTML (PowerShell)
```powershell
# Step 1 — get the download URL
$body = '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"get_screen","arguments":{"projectId":"11710553690432211807","screenId":"<SCREEN_ID>"}}}'
$r = Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "https://stitch.googleapis.com/mcp" `
  -Headers @{"X-Goog-Api-Key"="<KEY>";"Content-Type"="application/json"} `
  -Method POST -Body $body -TimeoutSec 30
$url = ($r.Content | ConvertFrom-Json).result.structuredContent.htmlCode.downloadUrl

# Step 2 — download the HTML (use WebFetch tool if DNS fails)
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri $url -TimeoutSec 30 | Select-Object -ExpandProperty Content
```

> **DNS note**: If `contribution.usercontent.google.com` fails to resolve, use the Cursor `WebFetch` tool with the download URL directly.

## Listing Available Tools
```powershell
$body = '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list","params":{}}'
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri "https://stitch.googleapis.com/mcp" `
  -Headers @{"X-Goog-Api-Key"="<KEY>";"Content-Type"="application/json"} `
  -Method POST -Body $body -TimeoutSec 30
```

## Workflow: Update a Page from Stitch
1. Fetch the screen HTML using `get_screen` + download URL
2. Extract structure: navbar, section layout, component markup, Tailwind classes
3. Map Stitch Tailwind color tokens → already present in `tailwind.config.js` (no changes needed)
4. Rewrite the React page component to match exactly
5. Run `node node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js build` to verify zero errors

## Generating New Screens
```powershell
$body = '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"generate_screen_from_text","arguments":{"projectId":"11710553690432211807","prompt":"<describe the screen>"}}}'
```
